---
description: Do not put a muted paragraph under a page or section title
globs:
  - apps/**/*.{tsx,ts}
alwaysApply: true
---

# No title leads

Do not place a muted paragraph under a page title or a section title to explain what the screen is doing.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<h1>{t("formCreateTitle")}</h1>
<p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{t("formCreateLead")}</p>

<EntityFormSection title={t("sectionSchedule")}>
  <p className="text-sm text-muted-foreground">{t("sectionScheduleLead")}</p>
</EntityFormSection>

// ✅ GOOD
<h1>{t("formCreateTitle")}</h1>
<FieldLabel required>{t("name")}</FieldLabel>
<InfoHint text={t("nameHint")} />
```

Field help goes through `InfoHint`, or the `hint` prop on `EntityDetailPanel` / `EntitySectionHead`.

Empty states, validation errors, and confirm-dialog copy stay. They are not title leads.
